# __APP_TITLE__ (`__PACKAGE_NAME__`)

**External module adapter** of the **__ZONE__** zone (`access: __ACCESS__`, tag `kind:external`).
Federation name `__FEDERATION_NAME__`, dev port `__PORT__`. Generated by
`pnpm gen:remote __ZONE__ __NAME__ --external`.

This remote is a thin React adapter: it renders `<ExternalModule>` from
`@org/mf-runtime/external`, which loads a vendor-built bundle and drives the **mount contract**
(`mount(el, props) → { update?, unmount }`, see `docs/external-modules.md` at the repo root).
The vendor can use any framework (or another React major); nothing is shared with the shell.

## Where the vendor bundle comes from

From this remote's `props.vendor` in the shell's `mfe-manifest.json`, **per environment** (never
in the build):

```json
"__FEDERATION_NAME__": {
  "entry": "https://cdn.example.org/__NAME__/mf-manifest.json",
  "props": {
    "vendor": {
      "url": "https://vendor.example/__NAME__/1.4.2/mount.js",
      "format": "esm",
      "integrity": "sha384-…",
      "timeoutMs": 15000,
      "config": { "<vendor setting>": "…" }
    }
  }
}
```

`format`: `esm` | `web-component` (+ `tagName`) | `script` (+ `global`) | `mf` (+ `remoteName`).
`config` is passed to the vendor as `props.config`.

In development the shell's generated `mfe-manifest.dev.json` points at the zone's **mock vendor**
(`tools/mock-vendor`, `__MOCK_VENDOR_URL__`, format `__VENDOR_FORMAT__`: a neutral demo widget),
and `src/features/external/utils/vendorConfig.ts` falls back to it when no config is set (standalone
mode). Production builds contain neither. Generated with another format:
`pnpm gen:remote __ZONE__ <name> --external --vendor-format esm|web-component|script`.
When the real vendor delivers, replace `props.vendor` (URL, format, `config`) in the shell's
`package.json` (`mfe.devManifest.remotes.__FEDERATION_NAME__.props.vendor`, then
`pnpm dev-manifest`) and per environment; the generic e2e checks keep working, the mock-vendor-only check
skips itself.

## Commands

| Command                                  | What                                                                     |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `pnpm dev:__ZONE__` (repo root)          | Shell + all __ZONE__ remotes + the zone's mock API and mock vendor (Nx task dependencies) |
| `pnpm exec nx dev __PACKAGE_NAME__`      | This adapter standalone on http://localhost:__PORT__ + mock API + mock vendor |
| `pnpm --filter __PACKAGE_NAME__ dev`     | This adapter only (start `pnpm --filter @org/mock-vendor serve:__ZONE__` yourself) |
| `pnpm --filter __PACKAGE_NAME__ build`   | Production build in `dist/`                                              |
| `lint` / `typecheck` / `test`            | ESLint, `tsc`, Jest                                                      |

## What the adapter passes to the vendor

| Prop                              | From                                                                     |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `basePath`, `path`                | shell mount (`__ROUTE_PATH__`) and the sub-path below it (vendor routes) |
| `theme`                           | shell theme (`useTheme()`), updates via `update()`                       |
| `user`                            | shell host prop `user`, reduced to `{ id, name, roles }`                 |
| `config`                          | `props.vendor.config` from the manifest                                  |
| `onNavigate`                      | shell router (relative = below `__ROUTE_PATH__`, `/x` = shell route)     |
| `onEvent`, `onError`              | demo "Events from the module" panel: replace with real handling          |

Loading/mount errors, timeouts, an incompatible `contractVersion` or a fatal `onError` show
`RemoteFallback` with "Try again"; the shell keeps working. Leaving the route calls the vendor's
`unmount()`.

## Layout

```
src/
  main.tsx                   standalone entry
  app/                       apps (exposed ./App), routes (one splat route)
  features/external/
    components/ExternalModuleHost/   the adapter (ExternalModuleHost.tsx, .module.scss, .test.tsx, index.ts)
    utils/vendorConfig.ts            dev fallback to the mock vendor (+ test)
    index.ts                         public API
  layouts/                   StandaloneLayout
  pages/OverviewPage         renders the adapter
```
